1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,640
This is MeteredPay, on testnet.

2
00:00:02,980 --> 00:00:06,200
Agents pay for every call — even the ones that fail.

3
00:00:06,820 --> 00:00:10,580
Say one in ten fails: that's money for work that never happened.

4
00:00:11,420 --> 00:00:14,440
MeteredPay only pays when the work checks out.

5
00:00:14,860 --> 00:00:15,660
Watch what happens.

6
00:00:15,660 --> 00:00:17,000
Watch this first.

7
00:00:17,320 --> 00:00:20,620
A call fails — and the held money comes straight back.

8
00:00:21,120 --> 00:00:22,160
Deducted: zero.

9
00:00:23,300 --> 00:00:27,960
The buyer puts down half a NEAR, and caps spending at point two.

10
00:00:28,360 --> 00:00:30,360
It can never spend past it.

11
00:00:30,660 --> 00:00:32,020
One document to check.

12
00:00:32,780 --> 00:00:38,100
The seller validates it against a schema — twelve words, eighty-nine characters.

13
00:00:39,200 --> 00:00:40,520
Valid — against the schema.

14
00:00:41,760 --> 00:00:42,380
First call.

15
00:00:43,100 --> 00:00:44,420
The check comes back valid.

16
00:00:45,200 --> 00:00:49,340
The buyer checks the receipt — same fingerprint, real signature.

17
00:00:50,260 --> 00:00:52,460
Only then does the contract take point one.

18
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:54,640
Now a call fails.

19
00:00:55,280 --> 00:00:58,940
The seller says so itself — error note, signed.

20
00:00:59,900 --> 00:01:03,520
The buyer files the claim, and the held point one comes back.

21
00:01:04,180 --> 00:01:05,840
Held, never taken.

22
00:01:06,780 --> 00:01:08,140
Deducted: zero.

23
00:01:08,780 --> 00:01:10,300
No answer in thirty seconds?

24
00:01:11,060 --> 00:01:13,700
The buyer's wait — the contract gives six hundred.

25
00:01:14,840 --> 00:01:17,340
Same deal: the money comes back.

26
00:01:17,900 --> 00:01:20,820
Then someone fiddles with a receipt — one letter changed.

27
00:01:21,620 --> 00:01:23,800
The buyer catches it, and pays nothing.

28
00:01:24,700 --> 00:01:26,180
Second good check.

29
00:01:26,720 --> 00:01:27,300
Checked.

30
00:01:27,500 --> 00:01:29,660
The same way — that's point two spent.

31
00:01:30,460 --> 00:01:31,560
The limit, reached.

32
00:01:32,560 --> 00:01:36,160
One more call — and the contract says no before any money moves.

33
00:01:36,960 --> 00:01:39,540
Over budget, refused, on the record.

34
00:01:40,440 --> 00:01:41,340
Balance untouched.

35
00:01:42,160 --> 00:01:45,720
One honest limit: this protects the buyer, not the seller.

36
00:01:46,380 --> 00:01:48,420
A dishonest buyer could still claim a failure.

37
00:01:49,220 --> 00:01:50,720
The buyer checks every receipt.

38
00:01:50,720 --> 00:01:53,760
The contract only pays on one the buyer has signed.

39
00:01:54,560 --> 00:01:58,500
MeteredPay. Failed call? Deducted: zero.

